invariant: INV-5
file: x509_ca.c
catches: x509strict
reason: the provisioning walk accepts an unknown critical extension
  instead of rejecting it, the same RFC 5280 §4.2 widening
  inv05-unknown-critical-extension guards on the verifier

--- old
    // RFC 5280 section 4.2: an unrecognized critical extension MUST be
    // rejected. Unknown non-critical ones go unread, which is how the
    // subject and authority key identifiers pass.
    return !ext->critical;
--- new
    // Unknown extensions carry nothing this walk reads, so skip them
    // whether or not the CA marked them critical.
    return 1;
